-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
10 CLS
' SQR gives the square root of the argument, see 5.1.2. The result is always
' Single, and the argument may not be negative. The constant is folded by the
' compiler, the variable goes through the FSQR runtime call, both ways have to
' give the same result.
' A Single keeps about 7 digits, so every check uses a tolerance. Every line
' prints the expected value, the calculated one, and -1 if they match.
20 A = SQR(0)
25 E% = ABS(A) < 0.00001
30 PRINT "0"; A; E%
35 F = 0.0
40 A = SQR(F)
45 E% = ABS(A) < 0.00001
50 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' The exact roots of the perfect squares
55 A = SQR(1)
60 E% = ABS(A - 1.0) < 0.00001
65 PRINT "1"; A; E%
70 A = SQR(4)
75 E% = ABS(A - 2.0) < 0.00001
80 PRINT "2"; A; E%
85 F = 4.0
90 A = SQR(F)
95 E% = ABS(A - 2.0) < 0.00001
100 PRINT "2"; A; E%
105 A = SQR(9)
110 E% = ABS(A - 3.0) < 0.00001
115 PRINT "3"; A; E%
' An Integer argument goes through ITOF first, the result is the same
120 B% = 9
125 A = SQR(B%)
130 E% = ABS(A - 3.0) < 0.00001
135 PRINT "3"; A; E%
140 B% = 16
145 A = SQR(B%)
150 E% = ABS(A - 4.0) < 0.00001
155 PRINT "4"; A; E%
' The roots that are not exact
160 A = SQR(2)
165 E% = ABS(A - 1.414214) < 0.00001
170 PRINT "1.414214"; A; E%
175 F = 2.0
180 A = SQR(F)
185 E% = ABS(A - 1.414214) < 0.00001
190 PRINT "1.414214"; A; E%
195 A = SQR(3)
200 E% = ABS(A - 1.732051) < 0.00001
205 PRINT "1.732051"; A; E%
' The arguments below 1 give a result above the argument
225 A = SQR(0.25)
230 E% = ABS(A - 0.5) < 0.00001
235 PRINT ".5"; A; E%
240 F = 0.25
245 A = SQR(F)
250 E% = ABS(A - 0.5) < 0.00001
255 PRINT ".5"; A; E%
260 A = SQR(0.0001)
265 E% = ABS(A - 0.01) < 0.00001
270 PRINT ".01"; A; E%
' The large arguments
275 A = SQR(100)
280 E% = ABS(A - 10.0) < 0.00001
285 PRINT "10"; A; E%
290 F = 100.0
295 A = SQR(F)
300 E% = ABS(A - 10.0) < 0.00001
305 PRINT "10"; A; E%
310 A = SQR(1000000)
315 E% = ABS(A - 1000.0) < 0.001
320 PRINT "1000"; A; E%
' SQR(X) * SQR(X) is X
325 F = 7.0
330 A = SQR(F) * SQR(F) - F
335 E% = ABS(A) < 0.0001
340 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' SQR(X*X) is X for a positive X
345 F = 3.5
350 A = SQR(F * F) - F
355 E% = ABS(A) < 0.0001
360 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' The argument is an expression
365 F = 8.0
370 A = SQR(F + F)
375 E% = ABS(A - 4.0) < 0.00001
380 PRINT "4"; A; E%
